# This machine's own settings. Copy to `.env` in the main checkout and fill in
# what applies; git ignores `.env`, and a worktree branched from here reads the
# main checkout's `.env` when it has none of its own (scripts/dotenv.mjs).
# A variable set in the shell wins over this file.

# --- Desktop build (apps/desktop) -------------------------------------------
# The Apple Development certificate in your keychain, so a build on this Mac
# is the same app to the keychain every time (docs/INSTALL.md, "The desktop
# app"). Without it the build is ad-hoc and asks for the keychain password on
# every install. Find the name with: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
#CSC_NAME="Apple Development: you@example.com (TEAMID)"

# A release build instead: a Developer ID certificate as a file, and its
# password. Notarised as well when the three APPLE_ variables are set.
#CSC_LINK=
#CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=
#APPLE_API_KEY=
#APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
#APPLE_API_ISSUER=

# --- Server (apps/server) ----------------------------------------------------
# A token of your own (8 characters or more), instead of the one the server makes
# for itself on first boot and keeps in its database. Either way clients send it
# as `Authorization: Bearer …`, and requests from this machine are not asked for
# it at all. Set this when the token must outlive the data directory — a
# container with a bind mount, say.
#SELFMP3_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Where the music and the database live; defaults are in apps/server/src/config.ts.
#SELFMP3_LIBRARY_DIR=
#SELFMP3_DATA_DIR=
#SELFMP3_PORT=4600
# One more address to publish with every snapshot, which the server cannot work
# out for itself: the HTTPS address of whatever stands in front of it — a
# Tailscale Funnel or a Cloudflare tunnel. The addresses it finds on this machine
# are all local and all `http://`, which is no use to a device somewhere else and
# is refused outright by the published app (docs/INSTALL.md, "Letting someone
# else in"). No trailing slash.
#SELFMP3_PUBLIC_URL=https://music.example.com
# Where you publish the app, if not the project's own Pages site: the server's
# page links there, and a public address lets that site call this server.
#SELFMP3_APP_URL=https://you.github.io/selfmp3
#SELFMP3_DOORMAN_URL=

# Smart features (docs/features/ai.md): any OpenAI-compatible endpoint that
# answers in a JSON schema. Unset, they are off and say so. ~/UofT/claude-api
# serves one on this Mac from your Claude subscription.
#SELFMP3_AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1
#SELFMP3_AI_API_KEY=
#SELFMP3_AI_MODEL_FAST=sonnet
#SELFMP3_AI_MODEL_SMART=sonnet

# A folder standing in for the bucket, for a server run without an account (the
# dev profile sets this; docs/SYNC.md). Relative to the data directory.
#SELFMP3_CLOUD_DIR=bucket
